Template: kerbridge-config/realm
Type: string
_Description: Kerberos realm for this deployment:
 KerBridge serves one Kerberos realm. Give it in upper case, for example
 EXAMPLE.SITE. KerBridge derives other values from it: the domain root, the
 DNS domain, the NetBIOS name, the short name of the domain controller, and
 two organizational units.
 .
 You cannot correct the realm later. It goes into the Samba database, and
 the permissions of every file carry an identifier from it. This is binary
 data in many places, and no edit can change it. To use a different realm,
 provision the domain again.
 .
 KerBridge writes the initial config files on the first installation only.
 If you leave this empty, it writes nothing.

Template: kerbridge-config/realm_invalid
Type: error
_Description: Invalid Kerberos realm
 A realm is a domain name with dots and no spaces, for example EXAMPLE.SITE.
 Your value is not a realm name.

Template: kerbridge-config/ldap_url
Type: string
_Description: LDAPS URL of the domain controller:
 KerBridge binds to this address. It accepts ldaps:// only, because plain
 LDAP and StartTLS send the bind password and each password write in clear
 text.
 .
 The proposed address uses a domain controller with the name "kerbridge" in
 the realm above. Change the host name if yours is different.

Template: kerbridge-config/ldap_url_invalid
Type: error
_Description: Invalid LDAPS URL
 The address must start with ldaps://. KerBridge refuses plain ldap:// and
 StartTLS. An address in that form fails later.

Template: kerbridge-config/tenant_id
Type: string
_Description: Cloud IdP tenant id:
 The Microsoft Entra ID tenant whose users this deployment admits. Give the
 tenant id as a UUID.
 .
 Leave this empty only for a host that does no synchronization and serves no
 sign-ins, for example an administrator machine with kerbridge-manage.
 KerBridge then writes the config files with no identity provider in them.
 .
 This is not a secret.

Template: kerbridge-config/broker_api_client_id
Type: string
_Description: Application id of the broker API registration:
 UUID of the broker's Entra app, usually named "KerBridge broker API".
 .
 The broker validates access tokens for this Entra application registration.

Template: kerbridge-config/public_client_id
Type: string
_Description: Application id of the workstation client registration:
 UUID of the client's Entra app, usually named "KerBridge public client".
 .
 The workstation agents sign in with this public Entra application
 registration.

Template: kerbridge-config/sync_client_id
Type: string
_Description: Application id of the synchronization registration:
 UUID of the sync Entra app, usually named "KerBridge sync".
 .
 kerbridge-sync reads the directory with this confidential Entra application
 registration. These dialogs never ask for a secret, on purpose.
 .
 Next step, after the installation: put the client secret of that app into
 /etc/kerbridge.secrets/idp/entra/credential, owned by root:_kerbridge and
 with mode 0640. Sync finds it on its next cycle and needs no restart. Do
 not use chmod 0600. Sync cannot read it.

Template: kerbridge-config/admission_group
Type: string
Default: KerBridge Allowed On-prem Users
_Description: Name of the cloud group whose members are admitted:
 Membership of this group admits an identity. KerBridge does not mirror the
 other users into the directory, and refuses each sign-in for them. Nothing
 works until a group with this name exists in the Entra tenant.
 .
 Any group is possible; this name is only a suggestion. When the realm is
 live, replace the name with the object id of the group in
 /etc/kerbridge/idp_entra.toml, so that a rename cannot point it elsewhere.
